<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICA'S NAAMSA ELECTS NEW PRESIDENT.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICA'S NAAMSA ELECTS NEW PRESIDENT.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Association of Automobile Manufacturers of South Africa announced on Thursday it had appointed Christophe Kopke as its president for the year 1997/98.</p>
<p>Kopke is chairman of the management board of Mercedes Benz of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>The association said Jim Miller, group managing director of South African Motor Corp, had been elected vice president for the year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
